# Hive and tasks
- `tasksBox` is `Box<List>`; date keys share it with reserved metadata. Exclude metadata from task iteration. Never clear user storage to fix migrations.
- Preserve `Task` typeId 0/indices 0–18 (fields 0–15 are legacy) and `TaskStep` typeId 1/indices 0–8. Append fields compatibly with defaults; regenerate generated adapters only for an authorized model change and review output.
- Confirm contracts in `docs/design.md` and `docs/details.md` before identity, migration, or duration changes. Preserve legacy descriptions (including phase/schedule encoding); don't incidentally restructure them.
- Identity must be immutable, not derived from title/order. Preserve legacy records, recurring-series identity, and reward formulas. Cover duplicates, reorder/completion, date boundaries, and restart/recovery where relevant.
- Keep null legacy steps distinct from an explicit empty list. Validate new AI estimates; don't disguise invalid input with legacy defaults. Default legacy null/zero duration only as the shared helper specifies; reject invalid new values.
- Use isolated temporary Hive storage in tests. Verify adapter round trips, migration/retry, and restart behavior when relevant.
